# Line endings (card C2).
#
# This checkout has core.autocrlf=true, so without these rules every Windows
# working tree gets CRLF copies of the POSIX gates. That is not cosmetic:
# a CRLF shebang plus CRLF 'set -eu' makes dash abort with
# "set: Illegal option -", i.e. tools/check_headers.sh and
# tools/check_windows_tu.sh stop working for exactly the developers who need
# them from Windows (through WSL). Verified: after a rebase re-checked these
# files out with CRLF, both gates died on their 'set -eu' line.
#
# Keep it to shell/python entry points; everything else stays on text=auto.
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.py  text eol=lf
